<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Nov trade gap $169 mln vs $192 mln in Oct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Nov trade gap $169 mln vs $192 mln in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	 Nov 96	 Oct 96		 Nov 95</p>
<p> Exports mln USD	 179	    155		     n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		   348	    347		     n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		 - 169	  - 192		     n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY-NOVEMBER)</p>
<p> Exports mln USD     1,615	   1,425		    n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		 3,576	   3,131		    n.a.</p>
<p> Balance	     - 1,961	 - 1,706		    n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Data refers to Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for the previous year are not available as the country was under an international trade embargo that was lifted on October 1 after nearly four and a half years.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
